WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.495
In under two minutes, you will plan a night of lights, and get driving routes.

00:00:04.495 --> 00:00:05.532
We start on the map.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.720
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:11.626 --> 00:00:14.057
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.057 --> 00:00:16.556
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:16.556 --> 00:00:17.907
Tap Use my location.

00:00:19.658 --> 00:00:22.026
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.026 --> 00:00:22.723
Tap Allow.

00:00:25.814 --> 00:00:27.345
Choose what you want to see.

00:00:27.345 --> 00:00:28.507
Tap the season button.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.264
Tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:35.073 --> 00:00:37.666
On a place you want to visit, tap the heart.

00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:38.243
Add three.

00:00:44.582 --> 00:00:45.409
Tap My night.

00:00:45.409 --> 00:00:50.016
Your stops are here, in a sensible driving order, with the miles and the time.

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:53.263
Tap Open route.

00:00:55.582 --> 00:01:01.381
Your maps app takes about nine stops at a time, so a long night is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:01.381 --> 00:01:03.802
Each route starts where the last one ended.

00:01:04.702 --> 00:01:06.537
Tick each stop when you have been there.

00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:11.867
Tap a route's button to open it in your maps app.

00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:13.452
Then tap the X to close.

00:01:15.419 --> 00:01:17.543
Tap Share to send your night to a friend.

00:01:19.191 --> 00:01:20.985
Tap the heart on places you like.

00:01:20.985 --> 00:01:26.208
Open route splits your night into routes of nine or fewer, each starting where the last one ended.

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:27.527
Tick off stops as you go.

00:01:28.927 --> 00:01:31.157
Next up: Weekly lights email.
